meta {
  name: Delete Product
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

delete {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/REPLACE_WITH_PRODUCT_ID
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  `DELETE /api/v3/products/{identifier}` — delete a product by Mongo ObjectId.
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 against disposable products on "David's Dev Account".

  ## 204 (not the spec's 200)
  `openapi_pimv3.json` declares `200` only. Live: **204 No Content**. A follow-up
  `GET /products/{id}` after deletion returns `404`. Matches `API V3.md`'s prose
  convention.

  ## SKU-as-identifier still rejected
  `GET /products/WC-TEST-FULL-001` (by SKU on the kept fixture) still returns `422`
  after this session created the product itself — rules out any theory that the
  identifier-flexibility claim from `API V3.md` applies to v3 (see `Get Product
  by ID.bru`).

  ## ⚠️ Critical hazard — DELETE /products/{id}/{path} deletes the entire product
  `DELETE /products/{identifier}/{path}` does **not** scope the delete to `{path}`.
  It deletes the **entire product** regardless of what `{path}` is. Confirmed two
  ways:
  1. `PATCH`'d `category_ids` onto a disposable product (confirmed linked via
     `GET .../categories`), then called `DELETE .../products/{id}/categories`
     expecting only the category links to be removed — instead the whole product
     was deleted (204, then `GET /products/{id}` returned 404, not an empty list).
  2. Repeated with a completely made-up subpath (`/totally_made_up_path_xyz`) on
     a second disposable product — same result: 204, whole product gone. The
     `{path}` segment is not inspected by the delete handler at all.

  **Implication for docs**: never document or suggest
  `DELETE /products/{id}/{subpath}` as a way to unassign a category, remove an
  asset, or clear any field. Flag to Plytix as a likely bug — a scoped-removal
  endpoint that isn't scoped. See "Subpath Delete Hazard" example below.
}

example {
  name: 204 - Standard Delete
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-08 against disposable product WC-TEST-DISPOSABLE-003 (id 6aa022d82b6fd055ffb7caa8, since deleted). 204 No Content with empty body. A follow-up GET on the same id returns 404.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6aa022d82b6fd055ffb7caa8
    method: delete
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 204
      text: No Content
    }
    headers: {}
    body: {
      type: text
      content: ''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 204 - Subpath Delete Hazard (Entire Product Deleted)
  description: CONFIRMED HAZARD live 2026-09-08. Despite the /categories path segment, the entire product is deleted — not just its category links. Identical 204 is returned for any subpath value, including completely made-up ones. Do not use this pattern to unassign categories or assets.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6aa022442b6fd055ffb7caa5/categories
    method: delete
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 204
      text: No Content
    }
    headers: {}
    body: {
      type: text
      content: ''
    }
  }
}
